  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis is a partial fix for #3601. The cause of the metadata errors is not proven, and the issue stays open.\n\n- `xtask/src/build_stop.rs` (new): the stop rule and the metadata diagnostic.\n- `xtask/src/exec.rs`: in a plan that runs one step at a time (quick), a failed step whose name ends in ` build (--no-run)` stops the plan. Before, only `debug build (--no-run)` stopped it. The summary lists each later step as `SKIP ... not run (build failed: <step>)`. The gate exits red, and the FAIL row names the build step.\n- `xtask/src/exec.rs`: a failed build step whose log has `found invalid metadata files for crate`, `E0786`, `found possibly newer version of crate` or `E0460` prints one `BUILD FAULT` block. The block names the crate of the error and says that the build output is bad, not the tests. It gives two commands to try, one at a time:\n  1. the same gate with `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4`;\n  2. `cargo clean -p <package>`, with the `-p` package of the step (`camcraft-ui` for the ui step).\n- The gate does not retry and does not clean by itself. The job budget rule (#2814) does not change.\n- Each stopped step gets a log with the one line `not run (build failed: <step>)`. `select::log_failed` reads that line as a failed step. Thus `cargo xtask gate quick --failed gate-logs/<run>` runs the build step and each stopped step (review of this PR). The summary row of a stopped step is `SKIP`, not `FAIL`, so the post-merge report and the light-lane note do not count it as a test failure.\n- The `BUILD FAULT` block shows only for a failed step whose arguments have `--no-run`. A test step whose output quotes E0786 gets no block.\n- `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md`: one paragraph says what quick does after a failed build, and how to rerun after a stop.\n- `docs/decisions/3601-gate-build-failure-stops.md`: the choices, the dropped options, and the reading of the seed lead (`xtask/src/seed.rs`).\n\n## Readings\n\n- Red first: with the old stop rule, `a_failed_per_crate_build_stops_the_plan_like_the_whole_gate_build` and `quick_plan_stops_after_a_failed_per_crate_build` failed (the suite step ran after the failed build). For the review fix: without the stopped-step logs and without the `--no-run` check, `quick_plan_stops_after_a_failed_per_crate_build` (the `--failed` part) and `a_test_step_that_quotes_a_metadata_error_gives_no_block` failed.\n- `cargo test -j 6 -p xtask -- --test-threads=6`: 301 passed, 0 failed (lib), all other xtask binaries green.\n- `cargo clippy -j 6 -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main --dry-run`: prints the plan, 1 step (`xtask unit tests`). An earlier body said 1168 steps: that was the batch fallback without `--base`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`xtask/src/build_stop_tests.rs`:\n- `a_failed_per_crate_build_stops_the_plan_like_the_whole_gate_build`\n- `metadata_errors_name_the_crate_the_jobs_and_the_package_to_clean` (the three error texts: E0786 for `accesskit`, E0786 for `test`, E0460 for `png`)\n- `an_ordinary_compile_error_gives_no_metadata_block`\n- `quick_plan_stops_after_a_failed_per_crate_build` (a quick `Run` on a temp fixture; the build fails on a bad cargo flag, so nothing compiles; then `--failed` on its log directory selects the build step and each stopped step)\n- `a_test_step_that_quotes_a_metadata_error_gives_no_block`\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real 16-job build that gives E0786 or E0460. The block is tested on log text only.\n- The lanes path (batch, release, and the quick fallback to batch) is not changed. Its prebuilds already stop the suites.\n- E0462 alone does not start the block (it came together with E0786 or E0460 in the reported runs).\n\nChangelog: none\nProcess change: yes\n\nRefs #3601\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n",
